[38;5;231m⏺[39m [1mSection 4 — Testing and tooling[0m

  [1mRunner: Node's built-in [38;5;153mnode --test[39m.[0m The repo has zero dependencies, no lockfile, and no [38;5;153mnode_modules[39m. Node's test
  runner and its [38;5;153mmock[39m helper cover everything here, so the repo stays dependency-free — [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m gains only a
  [38;5;153mscripts.test[39m entry. That's the whole tooling addition; you chose runner-only, so no linter or formatter.

  Layout: [38;5;153mtest/auth.test.mjs[39m, [38;5;153mtest/tracking.test.mjs[39m. Fakes are plain functions passed through the [38;5;153mdeps[39m parameter from
  Section 2 — no mocking library, no module interception.

  [1mWhat gets tested[0m — essentially the Section 3 table, since that's where the behavior is:

  - Success: returns [38;5;153m{ success, userId }[39m, and [38;5;153mtrack[39m was called with that exact [38;5;153muserId[39m.
  - [38;5;153mfetch[39m rejects → [38;5;153m{ success: false, error: "Network error" }[39m, [1mand [38;5;153mtrack[39m was not called.[0m
  - 401 → invalid credentials; 5xx → service unavailable; the two stay distinct.
  - 2xx with [38;5;153muserId[39m missing → malformed-response error, and [38;5;153mtrack[39m was not called.
  - [38;5;153mtrack[39m throws → [1mlogin still returns success.[0m This is the one I most want locked down; it's the assertion that keeps a
    dead analytics endpoint from breaking login.
  - [38;5;153mtrackLogin[39m posts the [38;5;153m{ event, userId, timestamp }[39m shape, and swallows its own fetch failure.

  [1mOne correction to Section 1.[0m I said [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m stays in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m. Working through the tests, that's wrong — [38;5;153mapp.js[39m
  touches the DOM at import time, so anything left in it is unreachable from Node, and [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m is pure logic that
  would go permanently untested. I'd move it to [38;5;153msrc/validate.mjs[39m and test it alongside the rest. It's six lines with no
  behavior change, and it makes [38;5;153mapp.js[39m genuinely DOM-only as Section 1 intended. Tell me if you'd rather I leave it and
  accept the gap.

  [1mWhat stays untested, stated plainly:[0m the DOM wiring in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m — the form listener, the element lookups, the [38;5;153mawait[39m.
  Testing it needs a DOM environment (jsdom or a browser runner), which means dependencies and a real jump in setup
  cost. Given the wiring is a dozen lines of glue, I'd verify it by hand in the browser rather than buy that
  infrastructure now. So "the tests pass" will mean the auth, tracking, and validation logic is correct — not that the
  page works. Worth knowing when you read a green run.

